* -------------------------------------------------------------------
* STEP X: Analyze similarity of revisits as session progresses (Hodgson-style)
* -------------------------------------------------------------------

* 1. Sort by user, session, and timestamp
sort user_id session_id timestamp

* 2. Tag revisits: a revisit is when a user sees the same product again in a session
by user_id session_id product_id: gen visit_number = _n
label variable visit_number "Visit number to product in session"
gen revisit = (visit_number > 1)
label variable revisit "1 = revisit to product in session"

* 3. For each revisit, count how many distinct products were seen since the first view
by user_id session_id: gen view_index = _n
by user_id session_id product_id: egen first_view_index_val = min(view_index)

* For each revisit, count distinct products seen between first view and this revisit (excluding revisited product)
gen n_products_since_first = .
levelsof user_id, local(users)
foreach u of local users {
    levelsof session_id if user_id == `u', local(sessions)
    foreach s of local sessions {
        preserve
        keep if user_id == `u' & session_id == `s'
        local N = _N
        forvalues i = 1/`N' {
            quietly {
                su revisit in `i', meanonly
                if revisit[`i'] == 1 {
                    local fv = first_view_index_val[`i']
                    local vi = view_index[`i']
                    local pid = product_id[`i']
                    preserve
                    keep if view_index > `fv' & view_index < `vi' & product_id != `pid'
                    egen n_distinct = nvals(product_id)
                    restore
                    replace n_products_since_first = n_distinct[1] in `i'
                }
            }
        }
        restore
    }
}
label variable n_products_since_first "Distinct products seen since first view of revisited product"

* 4. Compute Euclidean distance to the immediately previous product
by user_id session_id: gen price_prev  = price[_n-1]
by user_id session_id: gen pixels_prev = pixels[_n-1]
by user_id session_id: gen zoom_prev   = zoom[_n-1]
gen euclid_dist_prev = .
replace euclid_dist_prev = sqrt((price - price_prev)^2 + (pixels - pixels_prev)^2 + (zoom - zoom_prev)^2) if revisit == 1
label variable euclid_dist_prev "Euclidean distance to previous product (revisits only)"

* 5. Bin revisits by how far into the session they happen
* (based on n_products_since_first)
gen revisit_bin = .
replace revisit_bin = 1 if n_products_since_first <= 2 & revisit == 1
replace revisit_bin = 2 if n_products_since_first >= 3 & n_products_since_first <= 5 & revisit == 1
replace revisit_bin = 3 if n_products_since_first >= 6 & n_products_since_first <= 10 & revisit == 1
replace revisit_bin = 4 if n_products_since_first > 10 & revisit == 1
label define revisit_bins 1 "≤2" 2 "3–5" 3 "6–10" 4 ">10"
label values revisit_bin revisit_bins
label variable revisit_bin "Bin: # distinct products since first view"

* 6. For each bin, compute average distance and plot similarity
preserve
keep if revisit == 1 & !missing(revisit_bin) & !missing(euclid_dist_prev)
collapse (mean) avg_dist=euclid_dist_prev, by(revisit_bin)
gen similarity = 1/avg_dist
label variable similarity "Similarity (1/Avg Euclidean distance)"

* Bar chart: Similarity by revisit bin
graph bar similarity, over(revisit_bin) bar(1, bcolor(navy)) \
    ytitle("Similarity (1/Distance)") \
    title("Similarity of Revisits by Session Progress") \
    blabel(bar, format(%4.2f)) \
    legend(off)

* Show the table as well
list revisit_bin avg_dist similarity, noobs
restore

* -------------------------------------------------------------------
* END Hodgson-style revisit similarity analysis
* ------------------------------------------------------------------- 
